-- title:
--   Non-degeneracy of the full-kernel Vélu quotient at odd level
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number which is odd. The conclusion is the proposition `FullKernelDiscAt N`, which unfolds to the following assertion: for every algebraically closed field $L$ (in the lowest universe, with decidable equality) in which $2 \neq 0$, for every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $L$ that is elliptic, and for every point $Q$ of the associated affine curve $W.toAffine$ whose additive order `addOrderOf Q` equals exactly $N$, the discriminant $\Delta$ of the Weierstrass curve $W.fullKernelQuotient\ Q\ N$ is nonzero. Here `fullKernelQuotient` is the curve obtained by applying `W.veluQuotientOfSums` to the pair of Vélu sums formed over the finite index set $W.oddOrderSummingSet\ Q\ (N-1)$ of coordinate pairs $(x,y)$: the first argument is $\sum (W.veluGx\ x\ y)$ and the second is $\sum \bigl(x \cdot W.veluGx\ x\ y - y \cdot W.veluGy\ x\ y\bigr)$. Thus, over any algebraically closed field of characteristic different from $2$, the Vélu quotient of an elliptic curve by the cyclic group generated by a point of exact odd order $N$ is again given by a non-singular Weierstrass equation.
--
--   This is the non-degeneracy statement for the quotient of an elliptic curve by a cyclic subgroup of odd order $N$, computed by Vélu's formulas from a half-system of the kernel: the resulting Weierstrass equation again defines an elliptic curve. It is used, together with the modular-polynomial root property and the injectivity of the associated root map, in the bridge between cyclic subgroups of order $N$ and points of the modular curve, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelDiscAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelDiscAt) and [`ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelIsRootAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.TatePoint.fullKernelIsRootAt).
